From b2e60931b7463e4a28c24d1e8b81d479598f6abe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:33:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] venus: res_id frame-identity tracking (3 of 5 links
 working)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tracks the chain that names which buffer a submission rendered into, resolving
to a virgl res_id — the identity the host already holds an fd for, via
vtest_resource_import_blob. Better than matching on geometry, which cannot tell
the primary display from the virtual one and cannot identify the current frame
at all, since the display buffers are a fixed pool.

WORKING, measured live: memory->res_id (78 hits), image->memory (216 via
BindImageMemory2), view->image (171), submit (200+). NOT working: cmd->view.

WHAT THE MEASUREMENTS TAUGHT, and it cost three iterations: ANGLE uses the
MODERN variant of every entry point. vkQueueSubmit2 not vkQueueSubmit,
vkBindImageMemory2 not vkBindImageMemory. Hooking the legacy name leaves the
counter at exactly 0, which is indistinguishable from "not loaded" — so each
hook now announces its own first call rather than reporting only via submit.

STILL OPEN: no render-pass entry point fires. vkCmdBeginRendering,
vkCmdBeginRenderPass and vkCmdBeginRenderPass2 all stay at 0 while the display
is demonstrably compositing on this GPU (60% utilisation under animation). The
framebuffer hook DOES fire, so framebuffers are created — the begin is simply
not reaching these dispatches. Next suspects: secondary command buffers with
vkCmdExecuteCommands, or Venus batching command recording outside the per-call
dispatch path.

Off unless REMORA_VIDEO_CAPTURE=1.
